====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|surface of the Earth}} The [[surface]] of the [[Earth]], as opposed to the [[sky]] or [[water]] or [[underground]].
#: {{ux|en|Look, I found a ten dollar bill on the '''ground'''!}}
#* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=23|passage=If the afternoon was fine they strolled together in the park, very slowly, and with pauses to draw breath wherever the '''ground''' sloped upward. The slightest effort made the patient cough.}}
#* {{RQ:Christie Autobiography|II|4|passage=Mind you, clothes were clothes in those days. {{...}} Frills, ruffles, flounces, lace, complicated seams and gores: not only did they sweep the '''ground''' and have to be held up in one hand elegantly as you walked along, but they had little capes or coats or feather boas.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-08|volume=407|issue=8839|page=52|magazine=w:The Economist
|title=[http://www.economist.com/news/international/21579039-chinas-growing-empire-ports-abroad-mainly-about-trade-not-aggression-new-masters The new masters and commanders]
|passage=From the '''ground''', Colombo’s port does not look like much. Those entering it are greeted by wire fences, walls dating back to colonial times and security posts.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[terrain|Terrain]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1971|volume=|issue=|page=|magazine=Aircraft Engineering and Aerospace Technology
|title=The development of terrain following radar: an account of the progress made with an airborne guidance system for low flying military aircraft
|passage=As the terrain-following radar scans the '''ground''' ahead of the aircraft the actual clearance height is measured by the radio altimeter.}}
# [[soil|Soil]], [[earth]].
#: {{ux|en|The worm crawls through the '''ground'''.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} The [[bottom]] of a body of [[water]].
# [[basis|Basis]], [[foundation]], [[groundwork]], [[legwork]].
#* {{RQ:Skelton Complete|Hauke|62|lines=11–14|Wyth cry unreverent,<br>Before the sacrament,<br>Wythin the holy church bowndis,<br>That of our fayth the '''grownd''' is.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=An Humble Attempt to Put an End to the Present Divisions in the Church of Scotland, and to Promote Her Usefulness. {{...}}|passage=[B]e the consequences what they may, they shall not move an inch, nor a hair's-breadth from the '''ground''' of their groundless spiritual independence, {{...}}|year=1840|author=Lewis Rose|page=51|pageurl=https://www.google.ca/books/edition/An_Humble_Attempt_to_Put_an_End_to_the_P/66Cv-upW9nEC?hl=en&gbpv=1&pg=PA51|chapter=III|oclc=1113533477|publisher=George Gallie|location=Glasgow|url=https://www.google.ca/books/edition/An_Humble_Attempt_to_Put_an_End_to_the_P/66Cv-upW9nEC?hl=en&gbpv=0}}
# {{lb|en|chiefly|in the plural}} {{l|en|reason|Reason}}, ([[epistemic]]) {{l|en|justification}}, {{l|en|cause}}.
#: {{ux|en|You will need to show good '''grounds''' for your action.}}
#: {{ux|en|He could not come on '''grounds''' of health, or on health '''grounds'''.}}
# [[background|Background]], [[context]], [[framework]], [[surrounding]]s.
# {{lb|en|historical}} The area on which a battle is fought, particularly as referring to the area occupied by one side or the other.  Often, according to the eventualities, "to give ground" or "to gain ground".
# {{lb|en|figurative|by extension}} Advantage given or gained in any contest; e.g. in football, chess, debate or academic discourse.
# {{lb|en|in combination}} A place suited to a specified activity.
#: {{ux|en|a forest traditionally used as a hunting-'''ground'''}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1876|publisher=Great Britain. Parliament. House of Commons|journal=Parliamentary Papers|volume=14|page=147
|passage=I gather from your last answer that at the present time the constabulary, to a certain extent, is good recruiting '''ground''' for the army?}}
# The [[plain]] [[surface]] upon which the [[figure]]s of an [[artistic]] [[composition]] are set.
#: {{ux|en|crimson flowers on a white '''ground'''}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1819|author=Abraham Rees|title=The Cyclopædia
|passage={{...}} to pad a piece in diluted acetate of alumine to obtain a pale lemon '''ground''' {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1941|month=December|title=The Why and the Wherefore: Cornish names of G.W.R. locomotives|journal=Railway Magazine|page=575|text=''One and All'' is the motto of the County of Cornwall, used below the coat-of-arms, which is a shield embracing fifteen bezants, or golden roundels, on a black '''ground'''; [...].}}
# {{lb|en|sculpture}} A flat surface upon which figures are raised in relief.
# {{lb|en|[[point lace]]}} The net of small meshes upon which the embroidered pattern is applied.
#: ''Brussels '''ground'''''
# {{lb|en|etching}} A [[gummy]] substance spread over the surface of a metal to be etched, to prevent the acid from eating except where an opening is made by the needle.
# {{lb|en|architecture|mostly|in the plural}} One of the pieces of wood, [[flush]] with the plastering, to which [[moulding]]s etc. are attached.
#: {{ux|en|'''Grounds''' are usually put up first and the plastering floated flush with them.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[soccer]] [[stadium]].
#: {{ux|en|Manchester United's '''ground''' is known as Old Trafford.}}
# {{lb|en|electricity|Canadian|and|US}} An electrical {{l|en|conductor}} connected to the earth, or a large conductor whose electrical {{l|en|potential}} is taken as {{l|en|zero}} (such as a {{l|en|steel}} {{l|en|chassis}}).
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1961|location=Princeton, NJ|publisher=D. Van Nostrand|entry=GROUND|title=The International Dictionary of Physics and Electronics|edition=2nd|page=539|pageurl=https://hdl.handle.net/2027/uiug.30112067547296?urlappend=%3Bseq=549|text=А '''ground''' may be undesirable, inadvertent, or accidental path taken by an electrical current; or it may be the deliberate provision of conductors well connected to the ground by means of plates buried therein, or similar device.}}
# {{lb|en|electricity|Philippines}} [[electric shock|Electric shock]].
# {{lb|en|countable|cricket}} The [[area]] of [[grass]] on which a [[match]] is [[played]] (a cricket [[field]]); the entire [[arena]] in which it is played; the part of the field behind a [[batsman]]'s [[popping crease]] where he can not be [[run out]] (hence to ''make one's ground'').
# {{lb|en|music}} A composition in which the bass, consisting of a few bars of independent notes, is continually repeated to a varying melody.
# {{lb|en|music}} The tune on which [[descant]]s are raised; the plain song.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Richard 3|III|vii|text=''Buck''&#91;[[w:Henry Stafford, 2nd Duke of Buckingham|''ingham'']]&#93; &nbsp; The Mayor is here at hand; pretend ſome fear, // Be not you ſpoke with, but by mighty ſuit; // And look you get a prayer-book in your hand, // And ſtand between two churchmen, good my lord, // For on that '''ground''' I’ll build a holy deſcant: // And be not eaſily won to our requeſts: // Play the maid’s part, ſtill anſwer nay, and take it.}}
# The [[pit]] of a [[theatre]].
#* {{RQ:Jonson Bartholomew Fair|passage=the understanding gentlemen o' the '''ground''' here ask'd my judgment}}
# {{lb|en|India|obsolete}} {{syn of|en|munny||land measure}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1885|title=Manual of the Administration of the Madras Presidency|page=515
|passage=It is sub-divided into annas (or 16ths), of 3,600 square feet each; or when the land is for building purposes, into '''grounds''' (munnies) of 1/24 of a cawny each, as in the town of Madras.}}

