#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Bulk and Thin Film Synthesis of Compositionally Variant Entropy-stabilized Oxides| author=S Sivakumar; E Zwier; PB Meisenheimer…| journal=Journal of Visualized Experiments| year=2018| passage=Powder mixing and grinding are complete when the powder is homogenous and grey-black in color, appears finely '''ground''', and feels smooth.}}
# Processed by [[grinding]].
#: {{ux|en|lenses of '''ground''' glass}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Prehistoric Technology: An Experimental Study of the Oldest Tools and Artefacts from Traces of Manufacture and Wear| url=https://books.google.com/books?id=tkdLAAAAYAAJ| author=Sergeĭ Aristarkhovich Semenov| year=1985| page=14| passage=the traces of wear have the appearance of dull patches that look '''ground'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Proceedings of the Society of Antiquaries of Scotland| url=https://books.google.com/books?id=03YnAQAAMAAJ| year=2000| page=258| passage=The axial perforation, the handle socket and the quern base are all rough and do not appear '''ground''' or polished}}
#* '''2018''', H Glimpel, HJ Lauffer, A Bremstahler, ''Finishing Tool, In Particular End Milling Cutter'', US Patent App. 15/764,739
#*: An advantage of such a finishing tool is that, after the machining, the workpiece has high surface quality. The surface which is produced appears finely '''ground''' to polished by means of this procedure.

